A' represents a task or resource with a defined start and end point. A seco=
nd black line segment labeled 'B' overlaps partially with 'A', also indicat=
ing a start and end point.  In the left diagram, 'B' extends beyond 'A's en=
d, while in the right diagram, 'B' is entirely contained within 'A'.  In bo=
th, an orange line segment labeled 'B.start' marks the beginning of 'B'.  I=
ts end is determined by `min(A.end, B.end)`, calculated separately below ea=
ch diagram.  This calculation shows that 'B's end is truncated to match 'A'=
s end in the left diagram (`=3D A.end`), and 'B's end remains unchanged in =
the right diagram (`=3D B.end`). The dashed orange lines highlight the boun=
daries used in the calculation, visually demonstrating how the end of 'B' i=
s adjusted based on the relative positions of 'A' and 'B'." loading=3D"lazy=
" width=3D"624" height=3D"132" decoding=3D"async" data-nimg=3D"1" src=3D"ht=
