interval-overlaps/image-09-02-2-GSFUUA7K.svg" style=3D"color: transparent;"=
></div></figure>
<p>Therefore, when two intervals overlap, their overlap is defined by the r=
ange <strong>[<code>B.start</code>, <code>min(A.end, B.end)</code>]</strong=
>. Remember that in all these cases, interval A always starts first.</p>
<p><strong>Identifying all overlaps</strong><br>
Now, let=E2=80=99s return to the two arrays of intervals. Consider this exa=
mple:</p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display: flex; justify-content: left;"=
